{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ supplier.agreement_id }} - Manufacturing services agreement{% endblock %}
{% macro chrome(page_no, section) %}<div class="topline"></div><header class="head"><div class="brand"><img src="{{ logo_uri }}" alt="Caldova Pharmaceuticals logo"><div><b>Manufacturing services agreement</b><span>Caldova Pharmaceuticals, Inc. / {{ supplier.name }}</span></div></div><div class="meta">{{ supplier.agreement_id }}<br>{{ section }} · Page {{ page_no }} of 5</div></header><footer class="footer"><span>Confidential · Executed framework record</span><span>{{ corpus.fictional_notice }}</span></footer>{% endmacro %}
{% block body %}
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(1,'Agreement') }}<div class="kicker">Framework manufacturing services agreement</div><h1>{{ supplier.agreement_id }}</h1><p class="lede">Effective {{ supplier.agreement_effective }} between {{ agreement_common.customer_entity }} and {{ supplier.name }}.</p><div class="callout"><b>Purpose.</b> This agreement establishes commercial, operational, quality, and governance terms under which Caldova may issue product schedules and purchase orders for pharmaceutical manufacturing services.</div><h2>1. Parties and term</h2><p><b>1.1 Parties.</b> {{ agreement_common.customer_entity }} (“Caldova”) and {{ supplier.name }}, with its manufacturing site in {{ supplier.location }} (“Manufacturer”), enter this Agreement as independent contractors.</p><p><b>1.2 Term.</b> The initial term is {{ supplier.agreement_term }} from the Effective Date unless terminated earlier. Product schedules, amendments, quality agreements, and accepted purchase orders are incorporated by reference.</p><p><b>1.3 Order of precedence.</b> The applicable quality agreement controls GMP responsibilities; then a signed amendment or product schedule; then this Agreement; then an accepted purchase order. Supplier acknowledgments do not add conflicting terms.</p><h2>2. Governance and planning</h2><p><b>2.1 Joint oversight.</b> {{ agreement_common.governance }}</p><p><b>2.2 Forecasts.</b> {{ agreement_common.forecast }}</p><p><b>2.3 Purchase orders.</b> Each order identifies product, batch count or quantity, delivery dates, destination, storage and shipping conditions, and required release documents. Manufacturer shall promptly accept or identify a conflict.</p><div class="signature-grid"><div class="signature">Framework ID<br>{{ supplier.agreement_id }}</div><div class="signature">Supplier master ID<br>{{ supplier.vendor_id }}</div></div></section>
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(2,'Manufacture and supply') }}<h2>3. Manufacture and materials</h2><p><b>3.1 Performance.</b> Manufacturer shall use qualified facilities, equipment, systems, materials, and trained personnel to manufacture each scheduled product in accordance with cGMP, approved specifications, master records, applicable law, and written Caldova instructions.</p><p><b>3.2 Materials.</b> Manufacturer shall qualify and control purchased materials, maintain traceable inventory, use approved sources, and notify Caldova of shortages or suspected defects. Caldova-supplied materials remain Caldova property.</p><p><b>3.3 Site and subcontractors.</b> Manufacture is limited to the approved {{ supplier.location }} site. {{ agreement_common.subcontracting }}</p><p><b>3.4 Changes.</b> {{ agreement_common.change_control }}</p><h2>4. Testing, release, and delivery</h2><p><b>4.1 Batch package.</b> {{ agreement_common.release }}</p><p><b>4.2 Delivery.</b> Manufacturer shall release and make product available by the delivery date in the applicable order, packaged and labeled as specified. Title and risk transfer under the stated Incoterm.</p><p><b>4.3 Acceptance and rejection.</b> {{ agreement_common.rejection }}</p><h3>Batch evidence flow</h3><div class="flow"><div class="step"><b>Execute</b><span>approved master record</span></div><div class="step"><b>Test</b><span>approved methods</span></div><div class="step"><b>Review</b><span>deviations and records</span></div><div class="step"><b>Release</b><span>site quality disposition</span></div><div class="step"><b>Deliver</b><span>complete evidence package</span></div></div><p><b>4.4 Failure.</b> Manufacturer shall investigate failures, preserve evidence, notify Caldova promptly, and bear direct replacement manufacturing cost where its breach caused nonconformance.</p></section>
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(3,'Quality and regulatory') }}<h2>5. Quality responsibilities</h2><p><b>5.1 Quality agreement.</b> {{ agreement_common.quality_agreement }}</p><table><tr><th>System</th><th>Caldova responsibility</th><th>Manufacturer responsibility</th></tr><tr><td>Quality unit</td><td>Product requirements and final Caldova disposition</td><td>Independent site disposition and compliance oversight</td></tr><tr><td>Facilities/equipment</td><td>Approve product-specific fit</td><td>Qualification, maintenance, calibration, cleaning</td></tr><tr><td>Materials</td><td>Approve critical sources/specifications</td><td>Supplier qualification, receipt, testing, status control</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Approve methods and specifications</td><td>Method transfer, testing, data integrity, OOS control</td></tr><tr><td>Documentation</td><td>Timely review and decisions</td><td>Contemporaneous records and complete batch package</td></tr><tr><td>Change control</td><td>Approve product-impacting changes</td><td>Assess and notify before implementation</td></tr></table><p><b>5.2 Audits.</b> {{ agreement_common.audit_rights }}</p><p><b>5.3 Inspections.</b> Manufacturer shall notify Caldova promptly of regulatory inspections, observations, enforcement, or commitments that may affect a Caldova product or the approved site and allow reasonable review of relevant responses.</p><p><b>5.4 Records.</b> {{ agreement_common.records }}</p><p><b>5.5 Complaints and recalls.</b> The parties shall cooperate on complaints, investigations, field actions, and recalls. Cost follows documented responsibility for the event.</p></section>
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(4,'Commercial and risk') }}<h2>6. Charges and payment</h2><p><b>6.1 Charges.</b> Product-specific prices, transfer fees, capacity commitments, and permitted adjustments appear only in signed schedules or amendments. Manufacturer may invoice released batches and achieved milestones supported by required evidence.</p><p><b>6.2 Payment.</b> {{ agreement_common.payment_terms }} Caldova may withhold disputed amounts while paying undisputed amounts.</p><p><b>6.3 Records and audit.</b> Manufacturer shall retain records supporting invoiced amounts for at least seven years and provide reasonable access for verification.</p><h2>7. Risk allocation</h2><p><b>7.1 Warranties.</b> Each party has authority to enter the Agreement. Manufacturer warrants services will conform to applicable law, cGMP, approved requirements, and professional standards.</p><p><b>7.2 Insurance.</b> {{ agreement_common.insurance }}</p><p><b>7.3 Business continuity.</b> Manufacturer shall maintain and periodically test continuity plans addressing utilities, labor, materials, equipment, data, logistics, and critical suppliers; material disruptions require prompt notice and recovery estimates.</p><p><b>7.4 Indemnity and liability.</b> Each party is responsible for direct third-party claims caused by its negligence, willful misconduct, legal violation, or material breach. Neither party is liable for indirect or punitive damages except where prohibited by law or for confidentiality, fraud, or willful misconduct.</p><h2>8. Information and intellectual property</h2><p><b>8.1 Confidentiality.</b> {{ agreement_common.confidentiality }}</p><p><b>8.2 Ownership.</b> Each party retains background intellectual property. Caldova owns product-specific specifications, records, and know-how it supplies; Manufacturer retains general platform know-how. Product-specific improvements are documented in the applicable schedule.</p></section>
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(5,'Termination and signatures') }}<h2>9. Termination and transition</h2><p><b>9.1 Cause.</b> {{ agreement_common.termination }} Immediate suspension may occur for patient risk, critical quality failure, sanctions, fraud, or loss of required authorization.</p><p><b>9.2 Effect.</b> Manufacturer shall protect materials and product, complete or stop work as directed, return Caldova property and records, and cooperate in an orderly transfer. Accrued payment and confidentiality obligations survive.</p><h2>10. General terms</h2><p><b>10.1 Law and disputes.</b> This Agreement is governed by {{ agreement_common.governing_law }} law. Operational disputes escalate through the joint committee and then executive sponsors before formal proceedings.</p><p><b>10.2 Compliance.</b> Each party shall comply with anti-bribery, sanctions, labor, environmental, data-protection, and trade laws. Conflicts of interest must be disclosed.</p><p><b>10.3 Assignment and amendment.</b> Neither party may assign this Agreement without consent except to a successor in a permitted corporate transaction. Amendments must be written and signed by authorized representatives.</p><p><b>10.4 Entire agreement.</b> This Agreement and incorporated records are the complete framework understanding for their subject matter. Invalid provisions are replaced without invalidating the remainder. Counterparts and approved electronic signatures are effective.</p><div class="signature-grid"><div class="signature"><b>For Caldova Pharmaceuticals, Inc.</b><br>Charlotte Waltson · VP of Procurement<br>Signed {{ supplier.agreement_effective }}</div><div class="signature"><b>For {{ supplier.name }}</b><br>Alex Mercer · Chief Commercial Officer<br>Signed {{ supplier.agreement_effective }}</div></div><p class="notice">All entities, names, terms, and signature blocks in this agreement are fictional demonstration data and are not legal advice.</p></section>
{% endblock %}
